# Deploy an agent

Work from `/workspace/openbot`. Deployment publishes the source first, then
reconciles the remote runtime:

1. Commit the agent's source on a branch and push it:

   ```bash
   git switch -c <branch>
   git add configuration/
   git commit -m "<change summary>"
   git push -u origin <branch>
   ```

2. Open a pull request with the GitHub tools on your MCP server and share the
   link with the owner.

3. Deploy the agents:

   ```bash
   pnpm openbot deploy --yes --service agents
   ```

Deployment re-registers every authored agent against the deployed
agent-service URL and turns off local-runtime tunneling, so the owner's chats
reach the deployed endpoint instead of the local test process. After a
successful deploy, stop any `pnpm openbot dev` process you started for testing
and report the deployment result, including any pending authorization events.
